WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
01 · OVERVIEW: Know how your device thinks and stores data. Understanding hardware, file paths, and updates prevents lost coursework before deadlines.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
02 · HARDWARE: CPU calculates · RAM holds active apps · SSD keeps files. RAM clears when powered off; closing unused browser tabs frees active memory immediately.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.000
03 · FILE TREE: Use Term > Course > Subfolder hierarchies. Name files clearly like CS101_Lab2_Santos_v2.pdf instead of final_final2.docx.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.000
04 · 3-2-1 RULE: Keep 3 copies across 2 media with 1 off-device. Back up key drafts on your laptop plus cloud storage or an encrypted USB drive.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
05 · UPDATES: Patch only through built-in OS & app settings. Reject fake popup "driver updaters"; save work first, update, then restart properly.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.000
06 · TRY IT: Clean up one course folder and verify a backup today. Use Ctrl+S, Ctrl+Z, and check at least 15% free storage space for healthy performance.
